  "body": "Found while working #1036 (PR #1065), not reproduced yet.\n\n**Suspicion:** the planar ladder (`machining2d::descent::plan_core`, used by Bore and other 2D ops) takes the top of the cut from the feature's `entry_z` (the hole's mouth). If the stock stands more than the 2 mm plunge height above that mouth, for example a modelled hole whose top face sits below the stock top, or stock left by a skipped facing op, the first entry move starts inside the stock: a rapid or plunge into material.\n\n**Next step:** reproduce with a 2D op on a hole/pocket whose mouth is below a taller stock top, with nothing machined ahead. Check whether the verify laws (rapid-in-stock (d), the plunge law) already convict it. If a gouge or rapid-in-stock passes silently, raise to P0 and fix (the ladder's top from the prior stock, or refuse by name). If a law already catches it, pin that and close it, naming the law.\n\nDone means: a pinning test either way.\n",
